 "evidence": "A one-dimensional super-particle model of snow in a cloud, with Earth-fitted laws for growth, fall, sticking and fragmentation carried to lunar gravity and air through the fall speeds; one seed a case; a still cloud whose condensation feeds a set snowfall. Sizes for comparing the two worlds, not a forecast of single flakes.",
 "reading_rule": "Sizes are maximum dimensions of the snow arriving at the freezing level once the column has filled: the median, 90th and 99th percentiles by mass and the largest flake arriving at least once an hour on a square metre. snowfall_set_mm_h is the condensation the cloud is given, snowfall_mm_h what arrives; crystals_per_litre is the number entering at the cloud top; breakup false lets meetings that do not stick bounce whole."
